 ## Operating characteristics
--   **Time Complexity:** The computation is performed incrementally over $K$ frames. Each frame processes one ray direction for all voxels. The cost per voxel per frame depends on the number of samples along the ray, which is proportional to $R_\Omega / s$. Since $s$ increases with $\lambda$, lower-resolution blocks are processed faster [S1].
--   **Memory Complexity:** Requires storage for the packed volume, the reverse index texture, and the LAO accumulation texture. The LAO texture size is proportional to the number of voxels in the volume [S1].
--   **Performance:** The method achieves speed-up by combining multiresolution data reduction with adaptive sampling rates. The use of GPU fragment shaders and hardware blending allows for efficient parallel processing. Reported frame rates for LAO computation with 8 directions were comparable to diffuse illumination rendering (e.g., 27.2 FPS vs 26.4 FPS in the source results) [S1].
